# Real bug found integrating TheBot's harness on a Windows checkout:
# core.autocrlf=true (no .gitattributes to override it) silently converts
# every shell script to CRLF on checkout, which breaks its #!/bin/bash
# shebang inside the container ("cannot execute: required file not
# found") - a working script becomes non-executable purely from being
# checked out on Windows, with no error until a container actually tries
# to run it. Locks line endings to LF for anything with a shebang or that
# ships inside a Linux container image, regardless of the cloning
# machine's OS or local git config.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
